Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage
• provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name – filter records to Mountain View  
• provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name – filter to California (CA)  
• npi – count the number of distinct providers (NPIs)  
• healthcare_provider_taxonomy_1_specialization … healthcare_provider_taxonomy_15_specialization – hold the provider’s self‑reported specialization text; all 15 will be un‑pivoted into one list per NPI so that every specialization is counted  
• (optionally) healthcare_provider_taxonomy_code_[1‑15] – could be used to join to the taxonomy code tables but not required because the *_specialization columns already contain the text we need  

Typical conditions that will be used  
• LOWER(provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name) = 'mountain view'  
• provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name = 'CA'  
• specialization IS NOT NULL AND specialization != ''  

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory → complex queries
```sql
-- 1. Quick look at NPI rows that mention Mountain View in practice‑location city
SELECT npi,
       provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name AS city,
       provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name AS state
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.nppes.npi_optimized`
WHERE  LOWER(provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name) LIKE '%mountain view%'
  AND  provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name = 'CA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Verify the exact city strings that appear for Mountain View addresses
SELECT DISTINCT provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.nppes.npi_optimized`
WHERE  LOWER(provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name) LIKE '%mountain view%'
  AND  provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name = 'CA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect taxonomy specialization columns for a sample NPI in Mountain View
SELECT npi,
       healthcare_provider_taxonomy_1_specialization,
       healthcare_provider_taxonomy_2_specialization,
       healthcare_provider_taxonomy_3_specialization,
       healthcare_provider_taxonomy_4_specialization
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.nppes.npi_optimized`
WHERE  LOWER(provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name) = 'mountain view'
  AND  provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name = 'CA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Count how many distinct providers (NPIs) list Mountain View, CA as practice location
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT npi) AS mv_ca_npi_cnt
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.nppes.npi_optimized`
WHERE  LOWER(provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name) = 'mountain view'
  AND  provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name = 'CA';
```

```sql
-- 5. Un‑pivot the 15 specialization columns into one column for Mountain View providers
SELECT npi,
       specialization
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.nppes.npi_optimized`,
       UNNEST([
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_1_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_2_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_3_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_4_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_5_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_6_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_7_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_8_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_9_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_10_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_11_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_12_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_13_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_14_specialization,
         healthcare_provider_taxonomy_15_specialization
       ]) AS specialization
WHERE  LOWER(provider_business_practice_location_address_city_name) = 'mountain view'
  AND  provider_business_practice_location_address_state_name = 'CA'
  AND  specialization IS NOT NULL
  AND  specialization != ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Count distinct NPIs per specialization in Mountain View, CA
SELECT specialization,
       COUNT(DISTINCT npi) AS npi_cnt
FROM   (
        SELECT npi,
               specialization
        FROM   `bigquery-public-data.nppes.npi_optimized`,
               UNNEST([
